+#
+# "After proven cessation of the old execution and settlement of its known effects,
+# keep ordinary use gated if the resource still needs repair/reset. The host may admit
+# a fresh maintenance token generation for exactly that recovery operation."
+#
+# Review 2026-09-27T23-54-20Z made the reason concrete and it is a fact about THIS
+# module: `acquire` refuses every outstanding generation, so the recovery executor
+# cannot obtain its mandatory fresh generation while the old revoked token is still
+# held -- and the old token cannot be the gate, because returning it is precisely what
+# makes room for the recovery. Nor may the old token AUTHORIZE the fresh writer: a
+# revoked entitlement authorizes nothing.
+#
+# SO THE GATE IS A SEPARATE, DURABLE FACT ABOUT THE RESOURCE. It is admitted while the
+# old generation is still outstanding -- so there is no instant in which the resource is
+# ungated -- it survives that generation's return, it refuses every ordinary
+# acquisition, and it admits exactly one operation: the recovery this hold was taken
+# for. It is cleared by that recovery's own settled return and recorded result, never by
+# a caller saying it finished.
